+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// Live language for the Logros menu labels.
+//
+// The widget labels (combobox, texts, separators, reward checkboxes) are
+// plain strings stored in WidgetInfo at menu construction (AddMenuAchievements
+// above), so they used to keep the language active at boot until the next
+// restart, while the achievement lists (WIDGET_CUSTOM, drawn live via Tr())
+// followed the selector immediately. MenuDrawItem reads widget.name fresh on
+// every draw, so rewriting the stored names when the language CVar changes
+// is enough: the next frame draws the new language. No rebuild of the menu,
+// no custom widgets, no ImGui state churn — and nothing else is touched.
+//
+// The table below must list every label AddMenuAchievements() creates, in
+// the same EN/ES wording. Matching is by current name (EN or ES form), so it
+// works no matter which language the game booted with, and widgets this
+// table does not know are left alone.
+static const std::pair<const char*, const char*> kAchievementsLabels[] = {
+    { "Language", "Idioma" },
+    { "Each reward can be turned off", "Cada recompensa se puede apagar" },
+    { "Rewards", "Recompensas" },
